{
  "blocks": [
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**The problem.** Given the `root` of a binary search tree, return a **balanced** BST with the same values — one where, for every node, the heights of the two subtrees differ by at most one. Any balanced answer is accepted."
    },
    {
      "type": "drawing",
      "src": "/drawings/eae8d9ad-473f-46bd-9407-4cf0908229fc.svg",
      "alt": "The right chain 1, 2, 3, 4 has height 4. Its in-order list is 1, 2, 3, 4. Building from the middle gives root 2 with left child 1 and right child 3, and 4 under 3: height 3, and balanced at every node.",
      "width": 678,
      "height": 507,
      "scene": {
