    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Example"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "text",
      "code": "root = [1, null, 2, null, 3, null, 4]      ->  [2, 1, 3, null, null, null, 4]\nroot = [2, 1, 3]                           ->  [2, 1, 3]   (already balanced)"
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "1. In-order, then build from the middle"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "Two lessons glued together: the in-order walk gives the sorted values, and **Convert Sorted Array to BST** builds a balanced tree from them. Reuse the old nodes or create new ones — both are accepted."
    },
    {
      "type": "simulator",
      "program": "balance-bst",
      "caption": "Collect the values in sorted order, then each middle value becomes a root."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "code": "function balanceBST(root) {\n  const values = [];\n  const inorder = (node) => {\n    if (node === null) return;\n    inorder(node.left);\n    values.push(node.val);\n    inorder(node.right);\n  };\n  inorder(root);\n  const build = (lo, hi) => {\n    if (lo > hi) return null;\n    const mid = Math.floor((lo + hi) / 2);\n    return new TreeNode(values[mid], build(lo, mid - 1), build(mid + 1, hi));\n  };\n  return build(0, values.length - 1);\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "def balance_bst(root):\n    values = []\n\n    def inorder(node):\n        if node is None:\n            return\n        inorder(node.left)\n        values.append(node.val)\n        inorder(node.right)\n\n    def build(lo, hi):\n        if lo > hi:\n            return None\n        mid = (lo + hi) // 2\n        return TreeNode(values[mid], build(lo, mid - 1), build(mid + 1, hi))\n\n    inorder(root)\n    return build(0, len(values) - 1)"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "java",
      "code": "TreeNode balanceBST(TreeNode root) {\n    List<Integer> values = new ArrayList<>();\n    inorder(root, values);\n    return build(values, 0, values.size() - 1);\n}\n\nvoid inorder(TreeNode node, List<Integer> values) {\n    if (node == null) return;\n    inorder(node.left, values);\n    values.add(node.val);\n    inorder(node.right, values);\n}\n\nTreeNode build(List<Integer> values, int lo, int hi) {\n    if (lo > hi) return null;\n    int mid = (lo + hi) / 2;\n    return new TreeNode(values.get(mid), build(values, lo, mid - 1), build(values, mid + 1, hi));\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "code": "void inorder(TreeNode* node, vector<int>& values) {\n    if (node == nullptr) return;\n    inorder(node->left, values);\n    values.push_back(node->val);\n    inorder(node->right, values);\n}\n\nTreeNode* build(vector<int>& values, int lo, int hi) {\n    if (lo > hi) return nullptr;\n    int mid = (lo + hi) / 2;\n    return new TreeNode(values[mid], build(values, lo, mid - 1), build(values, mid + 1, hi));\n}\n\nTreeNode* balanceBST(TreeNode* root) {\n    vector<int> values;\n    inorder(root, values);\n    return build(values, 0, (int)values.size() - 1);\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Time O(n), space O(n)** for the list (plus O(h) recursion while reading the old tree)."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "2. Day–Stout–Warren: rotations, O(1) extra space"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "DSW rebalances **in place** with rotations. Step 1: rotate right at every node that has a left child until the tree is a right-leaning chain (the \"vine\"), in sorted order. Step 2: \"compress\" the vine with left rotations on every other node — first just enough to make the bottom level, then halving the chain again and again until it's balanced."
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "javascript",
      "code": "function balanceBST(root) {\n  const dummy = new TreeNode(0, null, root);\n  // 1. Tree to vine: rotate right until no node has a left child.\n  let tail = dummy, node = root, n = 0;\n  while (node !== null) {\n    if (node.left !== null) {\n      const left = node.left;              // right rotation at node\n      node.left = left.right;\n      left.right = node;\n      tail.right = left;\n      node = left;\n    } else {\n      n++;\n      tail = node;\n      node = node.right;\n    }\n  }\n  // 2. Vine to balanced tree: left rotations on every other vine node.\n  const compress = (count) => {\n    let scanner = dummy;\n    for (let i = 0; i < count; i++) {\n      const child = scanner.right;         // left rotation at child\n      scanner.right = child.right;\n      scanner = scanner.right;\n      child.right = scanner.left;\n      scanner.left = child;\n    }\n  };\n  let m = 2 ** Math.floor(Math.log2(n + 1)) - 1;   // nodes in the largest full tree that fits\n  compress(n - m);                         // the leftover nodes form the bottom level\n  while (m > 1) {\n    m = Math.floor(m / 2);\n    compress(m);\n  }\n  return dummy.right;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "python",
      "code": "def balance_bst(root):\n    dummy = TreeNode(0, None, root)\n    # 1. Tree to vine: rotate right until no node has a left child.\n    tail, node, n = dummy, root, 0\n    while node is not None:\n        if node.left is not None:\n            left = node.left              # right rotation at node\n            node.left = left.right\n            left.right = node\n            tail.right = left\n            node = left\n        else:\n            n += 1\n            tail = node\n            node = node.right\n\n    # 2. Vine to balanced tree: left rotations on every other vine node.\n    def compress(count):\n        scanner = dummy\n        for _ in range(count):\n            child = scanner.right         # left rotation at child\n            scanner.right = child.right\n            scanner = scanner.right\n            child.right = scanner.left\n            scanner.left = child\n\n    m = (1 << ((n + 1).bit_length() - 1)) - 1   # nodes in the largest full tree that fits\n    compress(n - m)                       # the leftover nodes form the bottom level\n    while m > 1:\n        m //= 2\n        compress(m)\n    return dummy.right"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "java",
      "code": "TreeNode balanceBST(TreeNode root) {\n    TreeNode dummy = new TreeNode(0, null, root);\n    // 1. Tree to vine: rotate right until no node has a left child.\n    TreeNode tail = dummy, node = root;\n    int n = 0;\n    while (node != null) {\n        if (node.left != null) {\n            TreeNode left = node.left;               // right rotation at node\n            node.left = left.right;\n            left.right = node;\n            tail.right = left;\n            node = left;\n        } else {\n            n++;\n            tail = node;\n            node = node.right;\n        }\n    }\n    // 2. Vine to balanced tree: left rotations on every other vine node.\n    int m = Integer.highestOneBit(n + 1) - 1;        // nodes in the largest full tree that fits\n    compress(dummy, n - m);                          // the leftover nodes form the bottom level\n    while (m > 1) {\n        m /= 2;\n        compress(dummy, m);\n    }\n    return dummy.right;\n}\n\nvoid compress(TreeNode dummy, int count) {\n    TreeNode scanner = dummy;\n    for (int i = 0; i < count; i++) {\n        TreeNode child = scanner.right;              // left rotation at child\n        scanner.right = child.right;\n        scanner = scanner.right;\n        child.right = scanner.left;\n        scanner.left = child;\n    }\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "code",
      "language": "cpp",
      "code": "void compress(TreeNode* dummy, int count) {\n    TreeNode* scanner = dummy;\n    for (int i = 0; i < count; i++) {\n        TreeNode* child = scanner->right;            // left rotation at child\n        scanner->right = child->right;\n        scanner = scanner->right;\n        child->right = scanner->left;\n        scanner->left = child;\n    }\n}\n\nTreeNode* balanceBST(TreeNode* root) {\n    TreeNode dummy(0, nullptr, root);\n    // 1. Tree to vine: rotate right until no node has a left child.\n    TreeNode *tail = &dummy, *node = root;\n    int n = 0;\n    while (node != nullptr) {\n        if (node->left != nullptr) {\n            TreeNode* left = node->left;             // right rotation at node\n            node->left = left->right;\n            left->right = node;\n            tail->right = left;\n            node = left;\n        } else {\n            n++;\n            tail = node;\n            node = node->right;\n        }\n    }\n    // 2. Vine to balanced tree: left rotations on every other vine node.\n    int m = 1;\n    while (m * 2 + 1 <= n) m = m * 2 + 1;           // nodes in the largest full tree that fits\n    compress(&dummy, n - m);                         // the leftover nodes form the bottom level\n    while (m > 1) {\n        m /= 2;\n        compress(&dummy, m);\n    }\n    return dummy.right;\n}"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "text": "**Time O(n), space O(1)** extra — no list, no recursion; only pointers change. Each rotation is O(1) and the total number of rotations is O(n)."
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Comparing the approaches"
    },
    {
      "type": "complexity",
      "rows": [
        {
          "approach": "In-order, then build from the middle",
          "time": "O(n)",
          "timeWhy": "One in-order walk to list the values, then each value becomes **one node**.",
          "space": "O(n)",
          "spaceWhy": "The sorted **list of all n values**, plus O(h) recursion."
        },
        {
          "approach": "Day–Stout–Warren: rotations",
          "time": "O(n)",
          "timeWhy": "Each rotation is **O(1)**, and the total number of rotations is **O(n)**.",
          "space": "O(1)",
          "spaceWhy": "No list and no recursion: only **pointers change**."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Edge cases to test"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "**Already balanced** — any balanced result is fine; approach 1 may change the shape.",
        "**A chain** — the worst input, height n.",
        "**A single node** — unchanged.",
        "**n = 2^k − 1** — the result is a perfect tree."
      ]
    },
    {
      "type": "heading",
      "text": "Variations"
    },
    {
      "type": "list",
      "ordered": false,
      "items": [
        "**Self-balancing trees (AVL, red-black)** — keep the tree balanced on every insert and delete with a few rotations, instead of rebuilding.",
        "**Merge Two BSTs** — two in-order lists, merge them, build from the middle.",
        "**Flatten a BST to a sorted linked list** — that's DSW's step 1 on its own."
      ]
    }
